 "note": "Caves House Hotel, Yallingup (1938-39, Principal Government Architect A. E. Clare, after the 1930 fire), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and the inHerit records. A big Inter-War Old English hotel of brick, about 40 m by 36 m, wings round a small service court: white-painted walls, steep terracotta tile hip roofs with cross gables, dark-stained half-timbering in the gables, tall chimneys, the terraced gardens falling away to the north-west. Marquees and the beer garden are on the south-west side. Metres: x left (south-west) to right (north-east) as seen from the south-east (the car park and Caves Road), y back (north-west).",
